error[Z0203]: `where` needs a condition that is true or false in every row, but this is a Column<Int>
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 | w.where(hours)
  |         ^^^^^ not a condition over the rows
  |
  = help: write a comparison or a Bool variable: `where(hours > 40)`, `where(female)`, `where(is_missing(hours))`

error[Z0203]: `where` needs a condition that is true or false in every row, but this is a single Bool
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 | w.where(true)
  |         ^^^^ not a condition over the rows
  |
  = help: a condition is an expression over the frame's variables, such as `hours > 40`; `is_missing(x)` tests for a missing value

error[Z0203]: `where` needs a condition that is true or false in every row, but this is NA
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 | w.where(NA)
  |         ^^ not a condition over the rows
  |
  = help: `x == NA` is always NA (section 4.1); `is_missing(x)` tests for a missing value

error[Z0101]: no variable `hour` in `w`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 | w.where(hour > 36)
  |         ^^^^ not a variable of w
  |
  = help: did you mean `hours`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"hours"`

error[Z0217]: the condition has 1 row and w has 3 rows
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:9
  |
3 | w.where(o["x"] > 1)
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^ a column of another frame
  |
  = help: a condition is built from the frame's own variables; `merge` joins frames (release 0.6.0)

